# DTF tier manifest: virtual-member-failure-policy
#   (artifact-keeper#4192 (+#4629), #4280/#4272, #4327, #4379; all fixed in
#   1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=mock-multi (a stdlib-python
# Helm / CRAN / RubyGems / NuGet upstream at 172.16.<slot>.91 whose first path
# segment picks healthy (/ok, /ok2) or failing (/fail -> 500)).
#
# A virtual repository's merged metadata must not silently lack a member that
# failed: a client reading a 200 index concludes the member's packages do not
# exist. And a member the merge CAN read must actually contribute.
#
# THE BUGS
# #4192  Helm `index.yaml`, CRAN `PACKAGES`, Hex and Bazel virtual merges
#        (`collect_virtual_metadata`) logged a member whose fetch or parse
#        failed and merged the rest: 200 without that member. Fixed: 502
#        naming the member and the cause; with `virtual_metadata_partial`
#        the healthy merge with `X-AK-Partial-Members`, `Cache-Control:
#        no-store`, `Warning: 199`; `ak_virtual_member_metadata_failures_total`
#        in both modes.
# #4280/#4272  RubyGems `specs.4.8.gz` is gzipped Ruby Marshal. A Remote
#        rebuilt it from cached gems only (an empty ~24-byte index) and a
#        Virtual JSON-parsed each member, failed and dropped it. Fixed: the
#        Remote passes the upstream bytes through, the Virtual decodes and
#        merges the Marshal, and a member it cannot read is a 502 naming it.
# #4327  A V2 NuGet upstream answering `index.json` with 403 (not 404) was
#        dropped as a virtual's member: missing from the virtual V2 feed and
#        404 on a V2 download through the virtual.
# #4379  The Galaxy metadata routes of a Virtual Ansible repository built
#        their documents from the virtual's own (absent) artifacts:
#        `versions/` was empty and the detail routes 404, so
#        `ansible-galaxy collection install` failed.
#
# RED image: ak-backend:1.10.0. GREEN: 1.11.0 and later.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: one admin login and ~60 API calls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: every Remote's upstream is the mock on a
# private address (the profile also sets it).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-multi"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
